  "id": "BIT-prometheus-2026-119566",
  "summary": "Prometheus through 3.15.1 Credential Leak via remote_write Cross-Host Redirects",
  "details": "Prometheus through 3.15.1 contains a credential leak vulnerability that allows attackers to capture Azure AD or Google IAM bearer tokens by redirecting remote_write requests to another host. Attackers controlling the remote-write endpoint or a redirecting server can return a 3xx to their host and replay the token, for example to write metrics to the victim's backend.",
